# The machines' depot in a region, cased at dusk and broken (docs/VISION.md §2),
# through real keys: walk to a working part, hold E with a steel edge in hand,
# and do it three times while the yard answers.
#
#   TOUR_FIXED_FPS=60 tools/tour.sh tours/works.tour --seed=1 --hour=18.5 --weather=clear:0 --held=axe_felling
#
# What it proves, in order: a depot stands in a region the plan is working, lit,
# with its mast over it; it PUTS BODIES OUT — one of its own from the gate and
# one on its round along the survey, with the coast itself calm, so what walks
# here walks out of this yard; its mast is read across the land at night AT THE
# ZOOM THE GAME IS PLAYED AT (the first version of this tour never looked at the
# depot after dark, and a review found the brightest thing in a night frame of
# the yard was a mob's health bar); standing in its yard is filed against the
# region's network without a word being said; each of its three housings is its
# own walk and opens under a steel edge; and when the third goes, the region is
# dark for good — the lights out, the frame before and the frame after of the
# same yard held to each other.
#
# What is NOT here: the land closing over the yard. That is four world days
# (Works.RECOVER_HOURS) and it is proved in tests/works/test_rules.gd, where the
# clock can be moved without three minutes of a runner standing still.

coast calm
place works
wait 0.8
await works 12
shot 01-a-depot-in-the-evening with works,works_lit,works_yard

# ITS OWN TRAFFIC. The coast is calm — nothing random is coming — so the body
# that walks out of the gate and the one that takes the survey line are this
# depot's (Works.OWN_EVERY, Works.PATROL_EVERY, both INF once it is dark). This
# is the half of "the region's machines come from its depot" that can be watched;
# the other half, a dark region rolling no machine of the plan at all, is counted
# in tests/works/test_in_game.gd.
await works_body 60
shot 02-the-yard-sends-one-of-its-own with works,works_lit,mob
await works_patrol 80
shot 03-a-round-along-the-survey with works,works_lit

# NIGHT, and the whole reason the mast is there. Backed off up the screen to the
# edge of the yard's own ground, AT PLAY ZOOM, and the picture itself is asked
# whether the machines' own light (works.gd STRIP) is really in it. Five tiles is
# about as far as this camera lets a depot be looked at whole — the frame is
# 26 tiles across and 18 deep, and past that the mast's head is all that is left
# of it (docs/ROADMAP.md: reading a thing off the horizon wants a camera change,
# not a taller mast).
hour 21.5
wait 1.2
walk 0,-1 1.0 run
wait 0.8
# Measured on main: 4640 pixels of the mast's own violet, and 3928 / 7372 /
# 10796 on branches cut before `evening` and `nights` changed what a night is.
# The claim counts LIGHT, so it must be measured on the commit it lands on, and
# it also swings with a wall-clock walk. 700 is under the lowest of the four,
# against a 30 that passed on a speck and the nothing an absent mast holds.
shot 04-the-mast-over-its-yard-at-night with works_yard,pixels:bebadf:700

# Its ground. Everything inside its reach answers to it, and the plan keeps a
# file on whoever is standing in the yard: nothing is written on screen about it
# — the horn over the land and the watchers turning are the whole of the telling.
place works
wait 0.8
await works_pressed 20
shot 05-standing-in-a-working-yard with works,works_lit

# The first housing. A steel edge and the key held: the housing's own lamp
# stutters while the work is on, and the plan hears about it the moment it opens.
press use 5.5
await works_part 14
shot 06-the-first-housing-open with works,works_open:1

# The second. Its own walk across the open, because no two of them can be
# reached from one spot (Works.PART_OFFSETS, held by tests/works/test_rules.gd).
place works_breaker
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_open:2 14
shot 07-the-second with works,works_open:2

# And the third, which is the one taken with the region already coming.
place works_coolant
wait 0.5
press use 5.5
await works_broken 14
wait 0.6
shot 08-the-yard-goes-dark with works,works_dark

# The same frame as the first, from the same place, so the difference is the
# thing and not the camera: every light on it out, and out tomorrow.
place works
wait 0.8
shot 09-dark-from-where-it-was-lit with works,works_dark
